# This file could be used for testing the API with Visual Studio Code

## Check the current session before login.
GET http://localhost:3001/api/sessions/current HTTP/1.1
###

## Get the public theater map.
GET http://localhost:3001/api/theater HTTP/1.1
###

## Login with username and password.
POST http://localhost:3001/api/sessions HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"mail": "gianni@example.com",
	"password": "password"
}
###

## Check the current session after login.
GET http://localhost:3001/api/sessions/current HTTP/1.1
###

## Enable TOTP mode for an admin user.
POST http://localhost:3001/api/login-totp HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"code": "371794"
}
###

## Logout.
DELETE http://localhost:3001/api/sessions/current HTTP/1.1
###

## Get my seats for the current user.
GET http://localhost:3001/api/my-seats HTTP/1.1
###

## Get all reservations as admin after TOTP.
GET http://localhost:3001/api/admin/reservations HTTP/1.1
###

## Direct reservation - client A.
## Use this with client B below to reproduce a conflict.
POST http://localhost:3001/api/reservations/direct HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"seatIds": [1, 2]
}
###

## Direct reservation - client B, same seats as client A.
## Expected result if client A already booked them: 400 with a clear error.
POST http://localhost:3001/api/reservations/direct HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"seatIds": [1, 2]
}
###

## Automatic assignment - normal category.
## Useful to check that the server assigns seats atomically.
POST http://localhost:3001/api/reservations/assign HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"count": 3,
	"category": "normal"
}
###

## Automatic assignment - premium category.
POST http://localhost:3001/api/reservations/assign HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"count": 2,
	"category": "premium"
}
###

## Modify reservation - valid example.
## Replace OLD_RESERVATION_ID with a real reservation id from /api/my-seats.
POST http://localhost:3001/api/reservations/modify HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"oldReservationId": 3,
	"seatIds": [3, 4]
}
###

## Modify reservation - stale data case.
## Run this after another client has already deleted or modified reservation 1.
## Expected result: 404 Reservation not found or 403 Not authorized.
POST http://localhost:3001/api/reservations/modify HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"oldReservationId": 1,
	"seatIds": [5, 6]
}
###

## Delete reservation - valid example.
## Replace RESERVATION_ID with a real id owned by the current user.
DELETE http://localhost:3001/api/reservations/1 HTTP/1.1
###

## Delete reservation - stale data case.
## Run this after another client already deleted the same reservation.
## Expected result: 404 Reservation not found.
DELETE http://localhost:3001/api/reservations/1 HTTP/1.1
###

## Re-booking cooldown test.
## Step 1: reserve seats 1 and 2.
## Step 2: delete that reservation.
## Step 3: immediately try to reserve seats 1 and 2 again.
## Expected result: 400 with "still on cooldown".
POST http://localhost:3001/api/reservations/direct HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
	"seatIds": [1, 2]
}
###

## Session check at the end.
GET http://localhost:3001/api/sessions/current HTTP/1.1
###